# Dashboard UI rules

You are editing the front-end of a FastAPI + ML serving app. The backend, model serving, MLflow integration, and `/metrics` endpoint already work — never touch them. Only edit HTML, CSS, JS/TS, and small client-side helpers.

The design target: an internal tool a senior ML engineer would actually use. Restrained, dense, monochromatic. Not a tutorial template.

## Files you may edit

- Main HTML/JSX template (entry point)
- CSS / Tailwind config / styled-components
- JS/TS rendering logic for the prediction form, batch panel, history table, monitoring panel

## Files you must not edit

- `app.py`, `main.py`, FastAPI route handlers
- Model loading or MLflow code
- Prometheus or `/metrics` plumbing
- Anything in `models/`, `data/`, `notebooks/`

## Stack discipline

- If the project uses a framework, keep using it. Don't introduce React if it's vanilla. Don't introduce Tailwind if it's plain CSS.
- Don't add dependencies unless the project already uses them.

---

## Color tokens (use these everywhere)

```css
:root {
  --bg:           #0B0D10;   /* page */
  --surface:      #13161A;   /* cards */
  --surface-2:    #1A1E24;   /* nested / inputs */
  --border:       #1F242B;   /* hairlines, 0.5px */
  --border-2:     #2A3038;   /* hover */
  --text:         #E6E8EB;   /* primary */
  --text-2:       #8A929C;   /* secondary */
  --text-3:       #5A626C;   /* tertiary, axis labels */
  --accent:       #8FB3FF;   /* periwinkle — single accent */
  --accent-dim:   #5C7FCC;   /* accent on hover/pressed */
  --ok:           #3FB950;
  --warn:         #D29922;
  --bad:          #F85149;
}
```

`--accent` is used **only** for: the primary "Predict" button, the line stroke in the hour chart, the bars in the weather/batch charts, and the confidence progress bar. Nowhere else.

## Typography

- Body: `Inter, -apple-system, system-ui, sans-serif`
- Mono: `'JetBrains Mono', ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace` — only for endpoint paths, latency numbers, model IDs, JSON
- Two font weights only: `400` and `500`. Never `600` or `700`.
- Sentence case everywhere. Never `MODEL READY`, never `BATCH PREDICTION`. Write `Model ready`, `Batch prediction`.
- All displayed numbers get `font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;`.

## Sizing scale

- Card titles: `13px / 500`
- Body: `12px / 400`
- Section eyebrows ("WHEN", "CONDITIONS"): `10px / 500`, `letter-spacing: 0.06em`, `text-transform: uppercase`, color `--text-2`
- KPI numbers: `26px–34px / 500`, `line-height: 1`
- Borders: always `0.5px solid var(--border)`
- Card radius: `8px`. Buttons and inputs: `6px`. Never larger than `12px` on cards.
- Card padding: `14px`. Grid gaps: `10–14px`.
- Page max-width `1280px`, centered, `24px` horizontal padding. Section vertical gap `16px`.

## Hard "don'ts" (these are the AI tells)

- No emoji. No icon libraries unless already in use.
- No `box-shadow` except a 1px focus ring on inputs.
- No gradient backgrounds anywhere.
- No status badges as colored pills with white text. Use a 6px dot + label.
- No `border-radius` larger than 12px on cards.
- No equal-width 3-column or 4-column grids for content of unequal importance.
- No placeholder helper text on self-explanatory fields.
- No animations beyond `transition: 120ms` on hover for buttons and inputs.
- No tooltips with paragraph-length text.
- No logo, no theme toggle, no settings panel, no login screen.

---

## Number formatting

Apply these helpers to every displayed number. Never show raw floats.

```js
const fmtInt  = (n) => Math.round(n).toLocaleString();
const fmtPct  = (x) => `${Math.round(x * 100)}%`;          // x in 0..1
const fmtMs   = (n) => `${Math.round(n)} ms`;
const fmtConf = (x) => x >= 0.8 ? 'High' : x >= 0.6 ? 'Medium' : 'Low';
```

Never display:
- More than 1 decimal in the UI
- Raw normalized inputs (0.62 etc.) — convert to real units first
- ALL CAPS labels
- Latency to 2 decimal places (`237.87 ms` → `238 ms`)

## Form ↔ model unit conversion

The model expects normalized 0–1 floats for `temp`, `atemp`, `hum`, `windspeed`. The user sees real units. Convert silently in the submit handler:

```js
const TEMP_MIN_C = -8, TEMP_MAX_C = 39;
const ATEMP_MIN_C = -16, ATEMP_MAX_C = 50;
const WIND_MAX_KMH = 67;

const payload = {
  season, mnth, hr, holiday, weekday, workingday, weathersit,
  temp:      (temp_c  - TEMP_MIN_C)  / (TEMP_MAX_C  - TEMP_MIN_C),
  atemp:     (atemp_c - ATEMP_MIN_C) / (ATEMP_MAX_C - ATEMP_MIN_C),
  hum:       hum_pct / 100,
  windspeed: wind_kmh / WIND_MAX_KMH,
};
```

Form labels must use human words (`Hour`, `Humidity`, `Wind`) and human units (`23 °C`, `14 km/h`, `45%`). Never raw column names (`hr`, `hum`, `windspeed`) or raw 0–1 floats.

