## Layout — top to bottom

### Section A — Header strip

One row, `padding: 16px 0`, `border-bottom: 0.5px solid var(--border)`.

- Left: title `Bike sharing demand` (15px/500), subtitle `MLOps serving · v1 · local` (11px/400, `--text-2`).
- Right: a single inline row of four status indicators, each = `<dot> Label`. Dots: 6px circle. `--ok` for API/Model/MLflow, `--warn` for Registry. Gap 14px. Font 11px, color `--text-2`.

Remove the four chunky pill badges entirely.

### Section B — KPI strip (4 cards, asymmetric)

Grid: `grid-template-columns: 1.6fr 1fr 1fr 1fr; gap: 8px;`

| Card     | Label              | Value                       | Sub                          |
| -------- | ------------------ | --------------------------- | ---------------------------- |
| 1 (wide) | Latest prediction  | `<rounded int>` rentals/hr  | inline sparkline of last ≤20 |
| 2        | Confidence         | `<int>%`                    | "High" / "Medium" / "Low"    |
| 3        | Avg latency        | `<int> ms`                  | `p95 · <int>`                |
| 4        | Predictions today  | `<int>`                     | `N batch · M single`         |

- Bg `--surface-2`. No border. Radius 8px. Padding 12px.
- Number font-size: 26px in card 1, 22px in others.
- Sparkline in card 1: 18px tall, accent stroke 1.5px, dot at the latest point.

Remove the existing 11-tile strip. Move Experiment, Registered Model, and Model Version into the result panel under a "Model" subsection.

### Section C — Single prediction (1.5fr) + Result (1fr)

Both cards: `border: 0.5px solid var(--border)`, radius 12px, padding 14px, transparent bg.

**Single prediction (left)** — two grouped sub-sections with eyebrow labels:

- **WHEN** — 3 cols: Season, Month, Hour (0–23). Below: Day, Holiday (toggle), Working day (toggle).
- **CONDITIONS** — 2×2: Weather (Clear / Mist + cloudy / Light rain or snow / Heavy rain or snow), Humidity (slider %), Temp (slider °C), Wind (slider km/h).
- Buttons: `Predict` (primary, accent bg, dark text) + `Load sample` (secondary, transparent + border). No "Reset".

**Result (right)** — stacked:

1. Eyebrow `Predicted demand` (11px, `--text-2`)
2. Big number `<int>` (34px/500) + `rentals/hr` (11px, `--text-2`)
3. `Confidence` label, 4px-tall progress bar (track `--border`, fill `--accent`, width = confidence%), % shown right
4. Hairline divider
5. Three label/value rows in mono: Latency (ms), Model (`v1 · local`), `vs typical <weekday> <hour>` (+/-% delta in `--ok` or `--bad`)

Remove the half-donut gauge entirely. Remove the four horizontal bars showing input features as percentages — they're inputs, not outputs.

### Section D — Two charts side by side (1fr 1fr)

**D1 — Predicted demand by hour**

Title + subtitle `<month> · <weather> · <day type>` (auto from form).

Behavior: on Predict, fetch 24 predictions (hours 0–23) with the rest of the form held constant.

SVG spec:
- viewBox `0 0 600 240`
- Y axis: 0 to ceil(max/100)*100, three tick labels (0, mid, max), 9px, `--text-3`
- X axis: ticks at 0h, 6h, 12h, 18h, 24h
- One faint dashed gridline at midpoint
- Line: `stroke: var(--accent); stroke-width: 1.5; fill: none`
- Filled circle at the selected hour with `<int> now` label
- No legend, no SVG-internal title, no decoration

**D2 — Demand by weather**

Title + subtitle `Same hour · same day · varying weather`.

Behavior: 4 predictions (weather 1–4), everything else from the form held constant.

SVG spec:
- Same axis treatment as D1
- Bars: width 40px, gap 20px, fill `--accent`. Opacity 0.95 for selected weather, 0.55 for others.
- Value (rounded int) above each bar in `--text` 9px
- X labels: `Clear`, `Mist`, `Light rain`, `Heavy`. Append ` (now)` to the active one.

### Section E — Batch prediction (full width)

Title row: `Batch prediction` + counter `<n> / 100 lines` right.

Two-column grid (1fr 1fr):

**Left — input**
- Eyebrow `JSON input · one object per line`
- Textarea: mono, 11px, padding 8px, height 110px, bg `--surface-2`, border 0.5px `--border`, radius 6px
- Buttons: `Run` (primary), `Load sample` (secondary)

**Right — result chart**
- Eyebrow `Predicted rentals/hour`
- SVG bar chart with real y-axis (0 to ceil(max/100)*100, three ticks), 0.5px gridline at midpoint, x-axis labeled with the **hour** of each prediction (from input row's `hr` field — not `1, 2, 3`)
- Bars: 40px wide, accent fill, value (int) printed above
- 9–20 predictions: drop value labels, 12px-wide bars
- 20+ predictions: just the line connecting bar tops

Below the two-column area, a results table (12px font, mono numbers, hairline row separators):

`# | Hour | Prediction | Confidence | Latency`

Remove the existing batch chart that renders 3 same-size blue squares.

### Section F — History (1.4fr) + Service health (1fr)

**History (left)** — title `Recent predictions`, sparkline 40px tall at top (accent line), then table:

`Time | Hour | Prediction | Confidence | Latency`

- Time in mono, `HH:mm:ss`
- Newest first, max 10 rows
- Hairline row separators only. No zebra striping. No card-in-card.

Fold the standalone floating sparkline into this card.

**Service health (right)** — title + counter `<up> / <total> up` right. Rows: `<dot> <Service name>` left, `<endpoint>` (mono, `--accent`) right. That's it.

Remove the chunky 2×4 grid of green/red rectangles.

### Section G — Evidence (full width)

Card shell. Title `Evidence` + counter `<available> / <total>` right.

Two sub-sections in the card, separated by a hairline:

- **AVAILABLE** (eyebrow): one row per file/endpoint, `✓ <name>` (12px, `--ok` check, `--text` name). Linkable if URL exists.
- **PENDING** (eyebrow — not "MISSING"): a single comma- or middle-dot-separated line in `--text-2`, 11px, `line-height: 1.7`. Not 7 individual red boxes.

This is the most important visual change in the whole dashboard. The 8 red tiles make the project look broken. A muted single line says "to-do" without screaming.

